From 4a96c05dd9da1dd0ed9dfe23a794a5cad9dbf96d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Heinz Wiesinger <heinz.accounts+anthropic@wiesinger.pro>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 21:06:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] DCTStream: Feed libjpeg more than one byte at a time

The source manager handed the compressed data to libjpeg one byte per
fill_input_buffer() call, i.e. with one callback and one virtual
getChar() call per byte of a possibly multi-megabyte image.

Read up to 4 KB at a time instead. This is not done for inline images,
since there the data following the image must not be consumed.

This saves about 5-8% when rendering pages dominated by JPEG decoding.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014HMJHMHEm38AikxhNxAjhE
